1
00:00:04,057 --> 00:00:10,063
My chocolate, my games, Momohiki!
Where are you?

2
00:00:10,147 --> 00:00:10,981
Huh?

3
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:17,487
Momohiki!

4
00:00:18,155 --> 00:00:21,033
I missed you so much!

5
00:00:24,036 --> 00:00:26,580
Hey, you feel kinda buff.

6
00:00:26,663 --> 00:00:28,915
What happened? Hmm?

7
00:00:28,999 --> 00:00:32,335
Anzu, dear, I saw you
having lots of fun with that hottie.

8
00:00:36,965 --> 00:00:40,093
I was thrown around by the plane,
and then thrown around in Times Square.

9
00:00:40,177 --> 00:00:41,428
It's been rough for me.

10
00:00:43,055 --> 00:00:44,556
What happened, Momohiki?

11
00:00:44,639 --> 00:00:46,850
You've transformed.
You're just like a person

12
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:50,062
in those ads that say,
"Weight Training Changed My Life."

13
00:00:52,689 --> 00:00:54,524
I guess
you don't need me anymore.

14
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:57,110
Goodbye to you, Anzu.

15
00:00:57,194 --> 00:00:59,321
Wait, Momohiki!

16
00:00:59,404 --> 00:01:05,285
It's not like that.

17
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:10,332
Momohiki…

18
00:01:13,251 --> 00:01:15,337
Hm, it's the alarm.

19
00:01:17,923 --> 00:01:18,924
Is it morning?

20
00:01:32,354 --> 00:01:33,355
A cat?

21
00:01:38,527 --> 00:01:39,361
My tongue…

22
00:01:41,363 --> 00:01:42,989
Quiet! You and that alarm!

23
00:01:43,073 --> 00:01:45,450
What… What… Wh-- What…

24
00:01:45,534 --> 00:01:46,868
Just so you know,

25
00:01:47,494 --> 00:01:49,621
you're the one
who made us stay up playing games,

26
00:01:49,704 --> 00:01:51,957
and then you dozed off
and you wouldn't let go of my hand.

27
00:01:52,874 --> 00:01:55,127
Thanks to you,
I was stuck here all night long.

28
00:01:55,877 --> 00:01:58,130
I don't remember.

29
00:01:58,213 --> 00:02:01,800
Wait a sec, was I sleeping
on his lap all night?

30
00:02:01,883 --> 00:02:04,010
Ah, I'm so embarrassed!

31
00:02:04,511 --> 00:02:05,971
Hold on! That's what embarrasses you?

32
00:02:06,054 --> 00:02:08,849
What about walking around
in an outfit like that?

33
00:02:10,016 --> 00:02:12,644
I'm so sorry. You must have been cold.

34
00:02:12,727 --> 00:02:14,271
My body's hurts.

35
00:02:14,354 --> 00:02:15,438
Ugh.

36
00:02:17,107 --> 00:02:20,610
It's nice out now.
I gotta go home and get ready.

37
00:02:21,528 --> 00:02:22,904
Time for serious self-reflection.

38
00:02:22,988 --> 00:02:24,447
REMORSEFUL: TO BE FILLED WITH REMORSE

39
00:02:28,243 --> 00:02:30,328
So, thanks for letting me stay here.

40
00:02:30,412 --> 00:02:33,957
Oh, huh, no worries,
I'm sorry about everything.

41
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:37,460
-See you.
-Okay.

42
00:02:41,173 --> 00:02:44,509
I meant to set my alarm
to go off way earlier than this.

43
00:02:45,302 --> 00:02:48,471
I wonder if Kazuki
will have enough time to…

44
00:02:48,555 --> 00:02:49,723
Oh, no, shoot!

45
00:02:49,806 --> 00:02:52,726
I can't believe I forgot
to give him his lunch!

46
00:02:54,186 --> 00:02:56,354
Guess I have to give it to him at school.

47
00:02:57,606 --> 00:02:58,857
-Here.
-Thanks.

48
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:00,609
Who does she think she is?

49
00:03:00,692 --> 00:03:02,569
She better not think
she can get away with this!

50
00:04:37,998 --> 00:04:41,209
#3: MY LIFE HAS BECOME A DATING SIM

51
00:04:45,463 --> 00:04:46,298
Mm…

52
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:48,633
So that means

53
00:04:48,717 --> 00:04:52,220
that I was holding
Kazuki's hand all night long, right?

54
00:04:53,305 --> 00:04:55,890
And I even slept on his lap.

55
00:04:59,894 --> 00:05:03,231
Wait a minute! I can't even remember
what time I dozed off.

56
00:05:03,315 --> 00:05:06,067
I do remember talking to that devil and…

57
00:05:06,151 --> 00:05:07,402
and that thing was…

58
00:05:07,485 --> 00:05:09,070
Who is…

59
00:05:09,904 --> 00:05:11,531
What is it? Uh…

60
00:05:12,157 --> 00:05:15,410
-Huh, Kazuki?
-Um…

61
00:05:17,704 --> 00:05:19,039
So, about my place…

62
00:05:22,417 --> 00:05:24,627
Aah… Are you kidding me?

63
00:05:24,711 --> 00:05:27,839
Did it sink in the Tokyo Bay or something?

64
00:05:32,552 --> 00:05:34,929
Maybe there's a weird plumbing issue
or something,

65
00:05:35,013 --> 00:05:36,931
because it seems like
only my unit was flooded.

66
00:05:37,015 --> 00:05:37,849
What?

67
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:41,061
My uniform
and textbooks are all drenched.

68
00:05:41,144 --> 00:05:43,355
Guess I gotta skip school today.

69
00:05:44,272 --> 00:05:46,775
Hey, um, can I borrow your phone?

70
00:05:46,858 --> 00:05:49,069
Oh, huh, sure. Go ahead.

71
00:05:49,152 --> 00:05:50,111
Great. Thanks.

72
00:05:54,783 --> 00:05:58,870
I know exactly who's responsible.
They caused this ridiculous situation.

73
00:05:58,953 --> 00:06:00,497
Water blast!

74
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:02,123
Yes. Thanks a lot.

75
00:06:03,083 --> 00:06:04,250
Gosh dang it!

76
00:06:04,751 --> 00:06:06,753
-Thanks for that.
-Oh, sure.

77
00:06:08,588 --> 00:06:09,422
So, everything's fine…

78
00:06:13,051 --> 00:06:14,844
Never mind. I take that back.

79
00:06:19,015 --> 00:06:20,934
Is there anything that I can do to help?

80
00:06:21,976 --> 00:06:24,479
Yeah, why don't you give me
your phone number?

81
00:06:24,562 --> 00:06:26,189
Huh? Sure.

82
00:06:26,272 --> 00:06:28,149
Hmm… Just a sec.

83
00:06:30,318 --> 00:06:31,152
Here.

84
00:06:31,653 --> 00:06:33,905
I'll call you
if anything comes up.

85
00:06:33,988 --> 00:06:35,073
Okay.

86
00:06:36,658 --> 00:06:40,328
-Oh, yeah, you forgot your lunch.
-Oh, thank you.

87
00:06:43,373 --> 00:06:44,916
You packed it really well,

88
00:06:45,792 --> 00:06:46,668
but, um…

89
00:06:46,751 --> 00:06:49,462
…did you have to use this bag?

90
00:06:49,546 --> 00:06:52,257
Oh, well, it seemed like
the perfect size.

91
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:53,675
And I couldn't bring you lunch.

92
00:06:54,384 --> 00:06:57,220
All of your fangirls
would think of me as their enemy.

93
00:06:58,221 --> 00:07:00,348
When I'm the one
who really made most of the lunch.

94
00:07:03,017 --> 00:07:04,686
Well, thank you.

95
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:07,814
Hoshino, you should get going.

96
00:07:07,897 --> 00:07:10,442
-Oh, ye-- Yeah.
-I gotta go.

97
00:07:10,525 --> 00:07:11,651
You've got this.

98
00:07:31,379 --> 00:07:33,214
Hey!

99
00:07:40,638 --> 00:07:43,224
I'm looking for a room
to move into right away.

100
00:07:49,314 --> 00:07:50,231
Huh?

101
00:07:51,858 --> 00:07:53,109
Can I help you?

102
00:07:57,572 --> 00:08:00,241
-Thank you very much.
-No problem.

103
00:08:03,661 --> 00:08:04,787
Hey, Anzu.

104
00:08:06,372 --> 00:08:09,000
-So, you brought your lunch today, huh?
-Yeah.

105
00:08:09,083 --> 00:08:12,086
You made that all by yourself? Awesome.

106
00:08:14,464 --> 00:08:16,591
Should I confide in Saki

107
00:08:16,674 --> 00:08:19,928
about the whole
complicated situation with Kazuki?

108
00:08:21,095 --> 00:08:25,266
But I don't wanna drag
my precious friend into this.

109
00:08:25,350 --> 00:08:27,810
BROKEN PHONE, CAN'T GET HOME,
MAJOR FLOODING

110
00:08:30,230 --> 00:08:32,190
-An unknown number's calling me?
-Oh?

111
00:08:32,273 --> 00:08:34,984
-Oh, you can eat.
-Okay.

112
00:08:35,068 --> 00:08:36,277
This is Anzu.

113
00:08:36,986 --> 00:08:38,905
Your scrambled eggs
are too sweet.

114
00:08:38,988 --> 00:08:41,032
It's a damn omelet!

115
00:08:41,115 --> 00:08:42,367
Oops, sorry.

116
00:08:43,451 --> 00:08:45,286
How are you calling?

117
00:08:46,287 --> 00:08:48,122
-Just bought a new phone
-What?

118
00:08:48,623 --> 00:08:51,251
Hey, are you free after school?

119
00:08:51,334 --> 00:08:54,587
Uh, well,
I don't have anything planned.

120
00:08:54,671 --> 00:08:57,799
Then, can you meet me
at Toutor by the station?

121
00:08:58,633 --> 00:08:59,676
Yeah, sure.

122
00:08:59,759 --> 00:09:01,928
All right, see you later.

123
00:09:02,595 --> 00:09:05,557
He hung up, jeez. Could have said more.

124
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:06,808
Your friend?

125
00:09:07,475 --> 00:09:10,228
Uh, yeah… Well, let's eat then.

126
00:09:12,272 --> 00:09:14,190
Wow, looks delicious.

127
00:09:14,274 --> 00:09:18,903
Sausages, sauteed spinach,
meat rolls, and scrambled eggs!

128
00:09:18,987 --> 00:09:20,321
It's an omelet roll!

129
00:09:21,155 --> 00:09:21,990
Hmm.

130
00:09:22,073 --> 00:09:25,326
So I guess he did end up
having to buy a new phone after all,

131
00:09:26,035 --> 00:09:30,623
even though he said he's broke.
Jeez, this is all my fault. I feel so bad.

132
00:09:31,958 --> 00:09:34,877
Wait! This is all that devil's fault!

133
00:09:35,878 --> 00:09:37,880
-All right, see ya!
-See ya!

134
00:09:38,881 --> 00:09:41,301
-Oh, teacher.
-Hm?

135
00:09:41,384 --> 00:09:45,221
I heard Tsukasa's house's flooded.
Is everything all right there?

136
00:09:45,305 --> 00:09:48,516
Oh, well, I was just about
to call him and find out.

137
00:09:49,142 --> 00:09:53,438
Oh, but I heard that
Tsukasa's phone was broken.

138
00:09:53,521 --> 00:09:55,356
What? But I think the number

139
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:57,817
he called from before
belonged to a cell phone.

140
00:09:57,900 --> 00:10:00,862
No way.
I guess he must've bought one then.

141
00:10:00,945 --> 00:10:02,113
All right, give me his number.

142
00:10:02,196 --> 00:10:04,782
-Well, I can't help you with that.
-You're a meanie.

143
00:10:05,366 --> 00:10:08,286
Well, Mister, I would still like
to hear that boy's voice.

144
00:10:08,369 --> 00:10:09,704
So put the speaker on.

145
00:10:09,787 --> 00:10:11,122
Hey! Come on!

146
00:10:11,205 --> 00:10:12,123
CONNECTED

147
00:10:12,206 --> 00:10:14,375
-Yes. Hello?
-What?

148
00:10:15,835 --> 00:10:19,631
Um, yes, hello there.
Have I reached Kazuki's cell phone?

149
00:10:20,298 --> 00:10:23,635
Huh? Kazuki's phone? No, uh…

150
00:10:24,552 --> 00:10:26,137
-No, it's not.
-Hm?

151
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,722
-Wait! What?
-Huh?

152
00:10:29,349 --> 00:10:30,224
Wha--

153
00:10:36,356 --> 00:10:38,191
This rent's expensive.

154
00:10:38,733 --> 00:10:41,152
-Hey, don't you think that guy next to us…
-Hm-mm.

155
00:10:41,235 --> 00:10:43,571
-…is way hot? Should I get his number?
-Hm?

156
00:10:45,823 --> 00:10:47,575
Man, I should have worn a hat.

157
00:10:49,827 --> 00:10:50,662
Huh?

158
00:10:50,745 --> 00:10:51,788
Uh…

159
00:10:55,792 --> 00:10:57,251
She's taking forever.

160
00:11:03,883 --> 00:11:04,967
Uh…

161
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:07,679
Hey, Tsukasa.

162
00:11:09,764 --> 00:11:12,308
I heard all about
what happened to your place.

163
00:11:12,392 --> 00:11:15,269
Oh, my gosh! It was so boring
without you at school today.

164
00:11:16,270 --> 00:11:17,980
Oh, there's an open seat.

165
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:21,109
Okay, I'm gonna go get something to drink.

166
00:11:23,986 --> 00:11:26,280
Uh, hey, sorry I took so long.

167
00:11:27,949 --> 00:11:30,785
Are you, um… Are you upset?

168
00:11:32,912 --> 00:11:34,288
Why did you bring them, too?

169
00:11:34,789 --> 00:11:37,291
Huh? Oh, well, I…

170
00:11:38,376 --> 00:11:40,211
-Ah!
-So why did Tsukasa make a call

171
00:11:40,294 --> 00:11:41,796
using your phone?

172
00:11:41,879 --> 00:11:43,673
Oh, well, he lives close.

173
00:11:43,756 --> 00:11:47,218
And he seemed like he needed help
this morning, so I let him borrow it.

174
00:11:47,301 --> 00:11:51,389
Ah, okay then. Will you tell him
to give me a call when he can?

175
00:11:51,472 --> 00:11:52,557
Um, okay.

176
00:11:54,934 --> 00:11:56,811
Are you going to see Tsukasa after this?

177
00:11:56,894 --> 00:11:58,730
What? Um, yeah…

178
00:12:00,606 --> 00:12:04,485
-My name's Rena Kashiwagi.
-And I'm Yukika Maezono.

179
00:12:04,569 --> 00:12:06,696
We're coming with you,
hope you don't mind.

180
00:12:09,574 --> 00:12:11,200
So, that's what happened.

181
00:12:15,288 --> 00:12:18,040
What? Hey, where are you going?

182
00:12:26,090 --> 00:12:28,009
-Huh, what are you…
-Just one today?

183
00:12:28,092 --> 00:12:29,010
Tsukasa?

184
00:12:29,093 --> 00:12:30,428
Uh…

185
00:12:30,511 --> 00:12:33,014
I only have plans to hang out with her.

186
00:12:33,848 --> 00:12:36,017
What? Wait, don't go, Tsukasa!

187
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:37,643
Huh? Um, hey…

188
00:12:48,154 --> 00:12:50,573
Hey, you sure? Isn't she your friend?

189
00:12:50,656 --> 00:12:54,160
Not really. She just follows me
around all the time.

190
00:12:54,660 --> 00:12:59,540
But, um, Kashiwagi, was it?
Doesn't she sort of have a thing for you?

191
00:13:03,753 --> 00:13:05,880
-I'm so over it.
-What?

192
00:13:06,672 --> 00:13:09,509
I'm nice because
she's a classmate of mine,

193
00:13:09,592 --> 00:13:12,595
but I'm not interested
in dating right now.

194
00:13:15,681 --> 00:13:17,099
Come to think of it,

195
00:13:17,183 --> 00:13:19,185
he was pretty cold
to that other girl, too.

196
00:13:20,061 --> 00:13:23,147
Jeez, I guess hot guys
have their own issues to deal with.

197
00:13:24,232 --> 00:13:26,275
Sorry. Bringing them was wrong.

198
00:13:29,070 --> 00:13:33,616
No, they forced you to bring them.
Sorry, I was harsh.

199
00:13:34,742 --> 00:13:38,663
That's okay. Yeah, it's hard
to set boundaries sometimes.

200
00:13:41,999 --> 00:13:43,709
-But…
-Hmm?

201
00:13:44,710 --> 00:13:47,630
You're not… you're not like them, huh?

202
00:13:48,464 --> 00:13:50,800
You didn't hound me
like everyone else does.

203
00:13:52,134 --> 00:13:54,262
So, it feels easy.

204
00:13:55,721 --> 00:13:56,973
Uh…

205
00:13:58,724 --> 00:14:01,727
Well, that's good then.

206
00:14:01,811 --> 00:14:04,397
Well, duh, I have hostages to save.

207
00:14:05,147 --> 00:14:06,148
Oh, hey!

208
00:14:06,732 --> 00:14:10,069
Kazuki, you said you don't want
to date anyone right now, right?

209
00:14:10,152 --> 00:14:11,320
Uh, yeah.

210
00:14:11,988 --> 00:14:13,990
Well, great, 'cause me too!

211
00:14:14,073 --> 00:14:16,284
I mean there are
far more important things than that.

212
00:14:16,367 --> 00:14:17,910
Oh, uh, okay…

213
00:14:18,619 --> 00:14:21,038
In other words,
even if he and I become friends,

214
00:14:21,122 --> 00:14:23,708
there's no chance
it will develop into a relationship.

215
00:14:23,791 --> 00:14:26,627
-That dumb devil chose the wrong cutie.
-Huh?

216
00:14:28,254 --> 00:14:29,755
Uh, hello?

217
00:14:30,423 --> 00:14:32,341
Oh, what'd you wanna talk about?

218
00:14:32,425 --> 00:14:34,260
Right, I-- I was wondering

219
00:14:34,343 --> 00:14:38,222
if I could temporarily
keep some of my stuff at your place?

220
00:14:38,306 --> 00:14:41,017
Of course.
Did you wanna bring it over now?

221
00:14:41,642 --> 00:14:43,352
I'm about to head off to work.

222
00:14:43,436 --> 00:14:45,479
But I have a realtor looking for a room.

223
00:14:45,563 --> 00:14:46,689
I see.

224
00:14:47,398 --> 00:14:49,442
His parents must live far away.

225
00:14:50,026 --> 00:14:52,320
Should I let him stay at my place again?

226
00:14:53,070 --> 00:14:56,574
That devil must've flooded Kazuki's place

227
00:14:56,657 --> 00:14:58,075
to make this whole thing happen!

228
00:14:58,576 --> 00:15:01,621
Then they kept him at my place
and broke his phone!

229
00:15:01,704 --> 00:15:03,998
It's too much drama to put on one person.

230
00:15:04,624 --> 00:15:07,418
Hey, I'll, um, reimburse you
for your phone,

231
00:15:07,501 --> 00:15:09,170
but I can't do it all at once.

232
00:15:09,253 --> 00:15:11,547
I'm thinking about
getting a part-time job soon.

233
00:15:11,631 --> 00:15:12,965
Huh?

234
00:15:16,218 --> 00:15:17,637
Oh, good, it's the realtor.

235
00:15:18,179 --> 00:15:19,305
-I'm sorry.
-It's cool.

236
00:15:19,388 --> 00:15:20,264
Yes.

237
00:15:21,766 --> 00:15:22,683
Hmm.

238
00:15:27,605 --> 00:15:29,565
So, it feels easy.

239
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:34,904
I thought the exact same thing
about him that night he stayed over.

240
00:15:36,739 --> 00:15:41,035
I will admit I kinda like that we feel
so comfortable around each other.

241
00:15:42,370 --> 00:15:43,537
What'd they say?

242
00:15:43,621 --> 00:15:46,207
Apparently, there aren't
any rooms available now.

243
00:15:46,290 --> 00:15:47,708
What?

244
00:15:47,792 --> 00:15:49,919
It seems
they all filled up recently.

245
00:15:51,045 --> 00:15:53,547
What if this was
that devil's handiwork, too?

246
00:15:54,131 --> 00:15:58,511
Good news is there will be one
opening up, but not for another month.

247
00:16:02,014 --> 00:16:03,849
You know, the cost of the phone

248
00:16:03,933 --> 00:16:06,811
is about the same price
as a month of rent.

249
00:16:08,187 --> 00:16:09,814
Hey, if it's cool with you…

250
00:16:09,897 --> 00:16:10,815
Huh?

251
00:16:11,857 --> 00:16:16,028
How about for a month, I stay
at your place and we call it even.

252
00:16:20,157 --> 00:16:23,828
What?

253
00:16:24,537 --> 00:16:28,165
Huh? Stay at my place for a month?

254
00:16:28,916 --> 00:16:31,794
I'm not asking you
to let me stay there for nothing.

255
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:34,714
I'll help out with the chores, of course.

256
00:16:34,797 --> 00:16:35,840
Chores?

257
00:16:36,632 --> 00:16:40,720
When I don't have work,
I'll make dinner and the next day's lunch.

258
00:16:40,803 --> 00:16:41,929
Uh, oh…

259
00:16:42,430 --> 00:16:45,224
And if "that thing" comes back,
I'll get rid of it.

260
00:16:45,307 --> 00:16:47,643
Roaches are unseemly,
so instead, cake.

261
00:16:47,727 --> 00:16:49,228
And as for me,

262
00:16:49,311 --> 00:16:52,231
it's close to where I work,
so it'll be a huge help.

263
00:16:53,357 --> 00:16:55,026
What should I do?

264
00:16:55,109 --> 00:16:57,528
His conditions
are too delicious to pass up!

265
00:16:57,611 --> 00:17:01,157
Uh, but still,
knowing that stinking devil…

266
00:17:01,741 --> 00:17:04,118
-Ouch!
-Um, let me see that.

267
00:17:06,245 --> 00:17:08,914
He'll just set up
insanely cheesy situations over and over.

268
00:17:08,998 --> 00:17:11,625
Oh, sorry!

269
00:17:11,709 --> 00:17:13,335
I didn't mean to, hon.

270
00:17:15,755 --> 00:17:18,758
That must be
their entire intention!

271
00:17:26,098 --> 00:17:29,185
My bad, um,
it's a crazy favor to ask of you.

272
00:17:29,268 --> 00:17:30,853
No, no, Not at all.

273
00:17:30,936 --> 00:17:34,023
If you're okay with it,
I don't mind having you stay at my place.

274
00:17:34,815 --> 00:17:36,192
That would be great.

275
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:41,697
Shoot! I responded impulsively
out of this sense of guilt.

276
00:17:42,573 --> 00:17:45,576
Would you explain it all
to your parents, too?

277
00:17:46,077 --> 00:17:47,912
No worries there.

278
00:17:47,995 --> 00:17:50,122
They won't have any issues with it.

279
00:17:50,206 --> 00:17:52,708
Sure, it's fine by me!

280
00:18:04,553 --> 00:18:06,180
That dream.

281
00:18:07,056 --> 00:18:10,768
Even I think it was pretty pathetic.
What a crazy dream.

282
00:18:11,602 --> 00:18:13,479
Me living with a hot guy.

283
00:18:16,982 --> 00:18:18,317
You're finally awake.

284
00:18:18,818 --> 00:18:22,363
It wasn't a dream.
It's all coming back to me now.

285
00:18:22,446 --> 00:18:23,739
Oh, wow, good morning.

286
00:18:23,823 --> 00:18:26,617
Morning. You've got an early bed hair.

287
00:18:26,700 --> 00:18:29,370
Yay! You're actually
making my lunch for me.

288
00:18:29,453 --> 00:18:31,288
Well, that was part of the deal.

289
00:18:36,544 --> 00:18:40,840
Amazing. I get to wake up
to a cutie making lunch in my kitchen.

290
00:18:42,133 --> 00:18:45,469
Seriously, hot guys are hot
no matter what they do.

291
00:18:46,929 --> 00:18:49,223
Kazuki, you're an early bird, huh.

292
00:18:49,306 --> 00:18:50,933
You just wake up late.

293
00:18:51,016 --> 00:18:52,143
Yeah.

294
00:18:52,226 --> 00:18:56,355
Now that I think about it,
he did seem to be really tired yesterday.

295
00:18:56,438 --> 00:18:58,107
-Long day?
-Yeah.

296
00:18:59,817 --> 00:19:01,944
I'm gonna take a bath and crash.

297
00:19:02,695 --> 00:19:05,573
First, he cleaned up
his totally flooded place,

298
00:19:06,198 --> 00:19:09,118
and then he did
like a million loads of laundry,

299
00:19:09,201 --> 00:19:11,245
and he had to be at work late.

300
00:19:12,121 --> 00:19:16,083
And after all that, he's still up
making us lunch this morning.

301
00:19:17,710 --> 00:19:20,129
-Hoshino, do you eat breakfast?
-Hm.

302
00:19:20,713 --> 00:19:21,839
Yes, I do!

303
00:19:21,922 --> 00:19:24,133
All right, then I'll make something quick.

304
00:19:26,468 --> 00:19:28,387
Thanks, Mom.

305
00:19:28,470 --> 00:19:29,388
Yeah, yeah.

306
00:19:30,973 --> 00:19:33,392
WEATHER FORECAST

307
00:19:34,101 --> 00:19:34,977
Here you go.

308
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:36,896
Yay!

309
00:19:36,979 --> 00:19:38,105
Time to eat!

310
00:19:38,606 --> 00:19:40,774
Ha, um!

311
00:19:42,484 --> 00:19:44,278
Oh, I need gym clothes.

312
00:19:44,361 --> 00:19:47,323
-Um, they were still drying.
-I'll go get them.

313
00:19:47,406 --> 00:19:50,910
-Um, can you pack my lunch for me?
-Yeah.

314
00:19:51,660 --> 00:19:54,663
I don't have to make lunch
or even breakfast.

315
00:19:54,747 --> 00:19:56,999
And he is a feast for the eyes.

316
00:19:57,082 --> 00:19:59,418
This might be a great situation after all.

317
00:20:00,377 --> 00:20:02,796
And I haven't seen
that devil around either.

318
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:04,340
Good morning!

319
00:20:04,423 --> 00:20:06,550
-Ugh, speak of the devil!
-Oh, jeez.

320
00:20:07,551 --> 00:20:11,972
Have you been enjoying
your oh-so-romantic dating-sim scenarios?

321
00:20:12,056 --> 00:20:14,725
Why don't you shut up?
You put Kazuki through too much!

322
00:20:14,808 --> 00:20:16,435
Be more considerate!

323
00:20:17,019 --> 00:20:19,104
Yeah, yeah, you say that,

324
00:20:19,188 --> 00:20:22,942
but you've been stuffing your face
with breakfast like a hamster.

325
00:20:23,025 --> 00:20:24,693
Shut up!

326
00:20:24,777 --> 00:20:26,362
And just so you know,

327
00:20:26,445 --> 00:20:29,406
Kazuki isn't interested
in dating anyone right now.

328
00:20:29,490 --> 00:20:32,868
Too bad! You chose the wrong guy!
You're a big stupid dummy.

329
00:20:36,747 --> 00:20:38,791
You're the stupid one, Anzu!

330
00:20:38,874 --> 00:20:42,753
Romance is unpredictable
because people always change their minds.

331
00:20:43,254 --> 00:20:47,174
And plus, did you forget what I told you?

332
00:20:47,841 --> 00:20:50,678
You're about to live
a dating sim-lifestyle

333
00:20:50,761 --> 00:20:52,805
surrounded by hotties…

334
00:20:52,888 --> 00:20:55,015
Oh, watch your step!

335
00:20:55,099 --> 00:20:56,934
…in real life.

336
00:20:59,645 --> 00:21:00,896
-Huh?
-Hm?

337
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:03,899
-Who's here so early?
-Ooh…

338
00:21:03,983 --> 00:21:05,901
Be right there.

339
00:21:06,568 --> 00:21:09,613
Hm? Our school uniform? Who is it?

340
00:21:10,281 --> 00:21:12,491
I'm not done, so don't disappear!

341
00:21:12,574 --> 00:21:15,202
-I still have a lot to say.
-Sure, sure!

342
00:21:15,286 --> 00:21:16,287
Coming.

343
00:21:18,872 --> 00:21:20,457
-Huh?
-Morning.

344
00:21:25,796 --> 00:21:27,047
How did you sleep, Anzu?

345
00:21:30,467 --> 00:21:32,970
Did you wake up late? Time for school.

346
00:21:34,847 --> 00:21:37,349
Who is this tall drink of water?

347
00:21:37,975 --> 00:21:39,310
Um… Uh…

348
00:21:40,978 --> 00:21:43,731
-Have we met somewhere before?
-What?

349
00:21:45,816 --> 00:21:48,319
Wait, what are you saying?
You still asleep?

350
00:21:49,611 --> 00:21:52,573
Don't tell me you forgot your old friend.

351
00:21:53,824 --> 00:21:55,492
My old friend?

352
00:21:55,576 --> 00:21:57,244
Hoshino, what are you doing?

353
00:21:58,329 --> 00:22:00,080
You should get going.

354
00:22:02,833 --> 00:22:03,667
Huh?

355
00:22:05,336 --> 00:22:06,211
Uh.

356
00:22:08,881 --> 00:22:11,759
Dearest Mom and Dad,

357
00:22:12,718 --> 00:22:15,220
how's life in the United States going?

358
00:22:16,347 --> 00:22:19,099
I've been forced
to live a sad and lonely life

359
00:22:19,183 --> 00:22:21,352
without my three greatest desires.

360
00:22:22,061 --> 00:22:27,191
But then a super hot guy became
my roommate which feels majorly awkward.

361
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:33,655
Next, a childhood friend
who I know absolutely nothing about

362
00:22:33,739 --> 00:22:35,199
suddenly appeared.

363
00:22:35,866 --> 00:22:39,787
And now, everything is about
to get awfully complicated.

364
00:22:42,915 --> 00:22:44,416
A fanfare, please!

365
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:46,543
And a big congratulations!

366
00:22:46,627 --> 00:22:48,796
Did you fall for my little trick?

367
00:22:48,879 --> 00:22:52,049
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

368
00:22:52,132 --> 00:22:55,594
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

369
00:22:55,677 --> 00:22:58,472
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

370
00:22:58,555 --> 00:23:00,849
Don't just let things be! Come on!

371
00:23:00,933 --> 00:23:03,519
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

372
00:23:03,602 --> 00:23:05,521
So I can make sure I get paid.

